</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem28' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem28TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.c</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(28);" >County Attorney's Office - Boulder County Community Planning &amp; Permitting Docket DC-24-0004: Text Amendments to the Code Related to Residential Uses, Boarding House, and Group Care or Foster Home</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(28, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment28' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43738" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Resolution 2026-032.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Resolution 2026-032.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>A resolution approving Boulder County Community Planning &amp; Permitting Docket DC-24-0004&#58; Text Amendments to the Land Use Code Related to<br>Residential Uses, Boarding House, and Group Care or Foster Home.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Cathy Peterson, County Attorney's Office</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem25' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem25TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.d</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(25);" >County Attorney's Office - Boulder County Community Planning &amp; Permitting Docket LU-25-0010/ESPR-25-0073: Turner Family Care Unit ADU and Accessory Structures</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(25, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment25' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43735" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Resolution 2026-028 Turner Family Care Unit ADU and Accessory Structures (LU-25-0010_ESPR-25-0073).pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Resolution 2026-028 Turner Family Care Unit ADU and Accessory Structures (LU-25-0010_ESPR-25-0073).pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>A resolution conditionally approving Boulder County Community Planning &amp; Permitting Docket LU-25-0010/ESPR-25-0073&#58; Turner Family Care Unit ADU and Accessory Structures</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Cathy Peterson, County Attorney's Office</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem37' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem37TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.e</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(37);" >Community Planning and Permitting - CDOT Agreement - CO 7 and 95th Street Local Match Contribution $1.3M</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(37, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment37' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43746" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC Memo and CDOT Agreement - CO7 and 95th 304545 .pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC Memo and CDOT Agreement - CO7 and 95th 304545 .pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>Staff from the Community Planning &amp; Permitting Department Transportation Planning Division and from the Public Works Engineering Division are seeking approval from the Board of County Commissioners to use $1.3 million in 2027 Transportation Sales Tax funds as the required local match for the CO 7 and 95th Street Multimodal Intersection Improvements Project. While Boulder County led project planning, development of the grant application, and coordination of the funding award, the Colorado Department of Transportation (CDOT) is responsible for the construction of the project. Approval of the local match will allow CDOT to utilize Transportation Improvement Program (TIP) funds awarded by the Denver Regional Council of Governments (DRCOG) and complete construction of this regionally significant multimodal transportation project.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Kelly Leadbetter, Community Planning and Permitting; Stacey Proctor, Community Planning and Permitting;</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem27' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem27TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.f</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(27);" >Community Services - Colorado Department of Labor and Employment Master Grant Agreement</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(27, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment27' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43737" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC_CDLE - CSD WfBC - Master Agreement IGA.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC_CDLE - CSD WfBC - Master Agreement IGA.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>The Master Grant Agreement between Boulder County and the Colorado Department of Labor and Employment serves as the master framework authorizing the County to operate all state and federally funded workforce development programs. The agreement does not include funding amounts, dates, or program specific details; those are provided separately through Notifications of Funding Allocation, work plans, and budget workbooks issued by Colorado Department of Labor and Employment. Because this agreement is used statewide across all ten local workforce areas, the coversheet is intentionally generic and does not list Boulder County or specific grant amounts. Approval of the agreement ensures Boulder County remains eligible to receive and administer Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act and other workforce grants each year, and supports County goals by maintaining access to critical employment, training, and support services for residents and enabling continued partnership with local employers to meet their hiring and workforce needs while ensuring compliance with federal and state requirements.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Erin Jones, Community Services</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem23' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem23TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.g</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(23);" >Community Services - Workforce Innovation Opportunity Act One Stop Operator Memorandum of Understanding with Colorado Department of Labor and Employment, Division of Vocational Rehabilitation</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(23, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment23' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43733" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC_DVR - CSD WfBC - WIOA MOU_2026-29.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC_DVR - CSD WfBC - WIOA MOU_2026-29.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>The Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act requires local workforce areas to maintain Memorandum of Understanding with all mandated one stop partners to outline how services will be coordinated across the workforce system. The Memorandum of Understanding defines each partner’s roles, responsibilities, referral processes, and contributions to the shared one stop center that serves jobseekers, workers, and employers. Approving the Memorandum of Understanding keeps Boulder County in compliance with federal and state requirements and ensures continued eligibility for Workforce Innovation Opportunity Act funding. The agreements support County goals by strengthening collaboration among agencies, improving access to employment and training services for residents, and providing employers with a coordinated system for meeting their workforce needs. Collectively, the Memorandums of Understanding help maintain an integrated and effective workforce system for the community.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Erin Jones, Community Services</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem35' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem35TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.h</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(35);" >Community Services - Workforce Innovation Opportunity Act One Stop Operator Memorandum of Understanding with Front Range Community College</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(35, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment35' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43743" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC_FRCC - CSD WfBC - WIOA_MOU_2026-29.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC_FRCC - CSD WfBC - WIOA_MOU_2026-29.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>The Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act requires local workforce areas to maintain Memorandum of Understanding with all mandated one stop partners to outline how services will be coordinated across the workforce system. The Memorandum of Understanding defines each partner’s roles, responsibilities, referral processes, and contributions to the shared one stop center that serves jobseekers, workers, and employers. Approving the Memorandum of Understanding keeps Boulder County in compliance with federal and state requirements and ensures continued eligibility for Workforce Innovation Opportunity Act funding. The agreements support County goals by strengthening collaboration among agencies, improving access to employment and training services for residents, and providing employers with a coordinated system for meeting their workforce needs. Collectively, the Memorandums of Understanding help maintain an integrated and effective workforce system for the community.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Erin Jones, Community Services</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem26' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem26TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.i</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(26);" >Community Services - Workforce Innovation Opportunity Act One Stop Operator Memorandum of Understanding with SER Jobs for Progress National, Inc.</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(26, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment26' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43736" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC_SER - CSD WfBC -WIOA MOU_2026-29.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC_SER - CSD WfBC -WIOA MOU_2026-29.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>The Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act requires local workforce areas to maintain Memorandum of Understanding with all mandated one stop partners to outline how services will be coordinated across the workforce system. The Memorandum of Understanding defines each partner’s roles, responsibilities, referral processes, and contributions to the shared one stop center that serves jobseekers, workers, and employers. Approving the Memorandum of Understanding keeps Boulder County in compliance with federal and state requirements and ensures continued eligibility for Workforce Innovation Opportunity Act funding. The agreements support County goals by strengthening collaboration among agencies, improving access to employment and training services for residents, and providing employers with a coordinated system for meeting their workforce needs. Collectively, the Memorandums of Understanding help maintain an integrated and effective workforce system for the community.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Erin Jones, Community Services</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem30' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem30TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.j</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(30);" >Human Services - 2026-2027 Connect for Health Colorado BCHS Grant Agreement</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(30, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment30' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43740" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='2026-27-connect-for-health-colorado-bchs-grant-cover-sheet.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >2026-27-connect-for-health-colorado-bchs-grant-cover-sheet.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>Revenue/Grant Agreement between Connect for Health Colorado and Boulder County to continue services for 2026-27.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Chandler Budlong-Springer, Human Services; Darlene Bushue, Human Services</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem20' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem20TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.k</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(20);" >Public Works - Bid Waiver for Boulder County Road Maintenance Asphalt Distributor Truck ($389,885)</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(20, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment20' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43723" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Bid waiver RM BearCat distributor truck_.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Bid waiver RM BearCat distributor truck_.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment20' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >2.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43724" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='FY 26 RM11 Q1 Budget Amendment Memo (005).pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >FY 26 RM11 Q1 Budget Amendment Memo (005).pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment20' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >3.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43725" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Sourcewell BOULDER COUNTY FLEET SERVICES-2026-4-10 (3) (1).pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Sourcewell BOULDER COUNTY FLEET SERVICES-2026-4-10 (3) (1).pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment20' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >4.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43726" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Sourcewell Etnyre contract.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Sourcewell Etnyre contract.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p><span>Public Works -&#160;</span><span>Bid Waiver</span><span>&#160;for&#160;</span><span>Boulder County Road Maintenance&#160;</span><span>A</span><span>sphalt D</span><span>istributor T</span><span>r</span><span>uck for </span><span>$389,885</span></p></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem24' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem24TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.l</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(24);" >Public Works - Bid Waiver for Frontier Fire to continue work on Recycling Center Pipe Repairs</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(24, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment24' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43734" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='PW Frontier Fire Bid Waiver 2026 (003).pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >PW Frontier Fire Bid Waiver 2026 (003).pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>Boulder County Building Services is requesting a bid waiver to award Frontier Fire the remaining scope to replace leaky fire sprinkler piping in the Recycle Center Processing Area for a total cost of $315,557.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Staff Contact(s)&#58;</strong> Joe May, Public Works</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem21' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem21TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >4.m</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(21);" >Public Works - Boulder County Road Maintenance Bid Waiver for 3 John Deer Road Graders ($ $1,328,180.74)        </a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(21, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment21' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43727" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Bid waiver 2026 RM Deere graders .pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Bid waiver 2026 RM Deere graders .pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment21' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >2.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43728" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='FY 26 RM11 Q1 Budget Amendment Memo (005)(1).pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >FY 26 RM11 Q1 Budget Amendment Memo (005)(1).pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment21' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >3.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43729" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Boulder County 772P Motor Grader_Detailed_Proposal_Quote_1269937.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Boulder County 772P Motor Grader_Detailed_Proposal_Quote_1269937.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment21' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >4.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43730" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Boulder County 772P Motor Grader_with Plow_Detailed_Proposal_Quote.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Boulder County 772P Motor Grader_with Plow_Detailed_Proposal_Quote.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment21' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >5.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43731" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='John_Deere_Contract_011723_(1).pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >John_Deere_Contract_011723_(1).pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p><span>Public Works - Boulder County Road Maintenanc</span><span>e Bid Waiver for 3 John Deer Road Graders</span><span>&#160;</span><span>(</span><span>$</span><strong><span>&#160;</span>$1,328,180.74</strong><span>)</span></p></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem8' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H2 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem8TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >5.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(8);" >Commissioners' Discussion Items</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H2><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV ><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem31' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem31TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >5.a</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(31);" >Commissioners' Office - Emergency Services Grant Program Advisory Committee (ESGPAC) Spring 2026 Funding Recommendations ($341,190)</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(31, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment31' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43748" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC Memo ESGPAC Grant Awards Recommendation 2026 Search and Rescue and Trail Safety Spring Grant Round-2.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC Memo ESGPAC Grant Awards Recommendation 2026 Search and Rescue and Trail Safety Spring Grant Round-2.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>Approval of the Emergency Services Grant Program Advisory Committee’s award recommendations for the Spring 2026 Search and Rescue and Trail Safety Grant Round. BOCC approval allocates $341,190 from the grant portion of the 2026 Emergency Services Sales &amp; Use Tax (Fund 151). ESGPAC met in April and May 2026 to review and make recommendations on grant proposals received by search and rescue and trail safety organizations for the 2026 Spring Grant Round.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Action Requested&#58;</strong> Decision</li>
<li><strong>Presenter(s)&#58;</strong> Barb Halpin, Commissioners' Office (In Person)</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem9' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H2 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem9TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >6.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(9);" >Confirmation of Executive Session Topics</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H2><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p><span>Confirming Executive Session topics noticed at the June 2nd, 2026 Regular Meeting were discussed as scheduled.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Action Requested&#58;&#160;</strong>Note for the Record</li>
<li><span><strong>Presenter(s)&#58;</strong>&#160;Natalie Springett, Commissioners' Office (In Person)</span></li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem10' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H2 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem10TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >7.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(10);" >Authorization for Executive Session</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H2><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>Authorization for the Board of County Commissioners to go into Executive Session on Wednesday, June 10th, 2026, at 1&#58;00 p.m., pursuant to C.R.S. 24-6-402(4)(b), legal advice, regarding the following topic&#58; Potential amicus brief in American Association of Nurse Practitioners v. McMahon, D.C. District Court Case No. 26-cv-01780.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Action Requested&#58;&#160;</strong>Decision</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem16' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H2 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem16TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >8.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(16);" >Public Hearing on Parks and Open Space Real Estate Acquisitions</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H2><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p><span>Parks and Open Space Department&#58; Real estate acquisitions monthly meeting.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span><strong>Location&#58;</strong> Hybrid (Hearing Room and Zoom Webinar)</span></li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV ><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem32' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem32TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >8.a</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(32);" >Parks and Open Space - Woodley Conservation Easement - 2026 CDOT Taking for CO Hwy 7 Widening</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(32, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment32' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43741" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Final_Woodley CE - 2026 CDOT Taking BoCC Memo Signed.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Final_Woodley CE - 2026 CDOT Taking BoCC Memo Signed.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>Colorado Department of Transportation proposes to acquire fee title to 0.09 acres of the Woodley property for the purpose of a highway widening project on CO Highway 7 (Arapahoe Road). The Property is encumbered by a conservation easement conveyed to the county in 2006. The Property is owned by Chris and Jennifer Anderson and is located at 7957 Arapahoe Road at the intersection of Arapahoe Road and Willow Creek Drive. A partial release of the conservation easement is necessary for the area impacted by this acquisition. Staff support this partial release of the 0.09 acres encumbered by the conservation easement because CDOT has condemnation authority over Boulder County.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Action Requested&#58;</strong> Decision</li>
<li><strong>Presenter(s)&#58;</strong> Michael Sylvester, Parks and Open Space (In Person)</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem34' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem34TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >8.b</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(34);" >Parks and Open Space - Montgomery-2026 City of Longmont Taking</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(34, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment34' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43742" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Montgomery-2026 City of Longmont Taking BOCC Memo6.9.26.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Montgomery-2026 City of Longmont Taking BOCC Memo6.9.26.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p>The City of Longmont proposes to acquire a permanent non-exclusive easement over 369 square feet or 0.009 acres of the Montgomery open space property to construct a bore entry point for emergency overflow of the City’s Montgomery Water Tank Replacement Project. The Property is located approximately 2 miles east of Lyons, south of Hwy 66 near the intersections of Hwy 66 and N. 53rd Street. Staff support this granting this easement because the requestor has condemnation authority over Boulder County.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Action Requested&#58;</strong> Decision</li>
<li><strong>Presenter(s)&#58;</strong> Tina Burghardt, Parks and Open Space (In Person)</li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem17' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H2 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem17TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >9.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(17);" >Public Hearing on Petition for the Organization of the Summerlin Public Improvement District of Boulder County</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H2><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(17, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment17' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43745" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='Resolution 2026-34 Summerlin PID on ballot.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >Resolution 2026-34 Summerlin PID on ballot.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p><span>County Attorney’s Office&#58; Public Hearing pursuant to C.R.S. § 30-20-508 to consider the petitions to organize the Summerlin Public Improvement District of Boulder County for the purposes of resurfacing public roads within the Summerlin neighborhood in unincorporated Boulder County. Email Robert Jacobs at </span><a href="mailto&#58;rjacobs@bouldercounty.gov"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="76041c1715191405361419031a12130415190318020f58111900">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><span> for more information.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span><strong>Action Requested&#58;&#160;</strong>Decision</span></li>
<li><span><span><strong>Presenter(s)&#58; </strong>Dan DeLange, Public Works&#160;(In Person); Olivia Lucas, County Attorney's Office (In Person)</span></span></li>
<li><span><strong>Location&#58; </strong>Hybrid (Hearing Room and Zoom Webinar)</span></li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem18' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H2 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem18TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >10.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(18);" >1:00 p.m. Afternoon Session</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H2><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><ul>
<li><strong data-ogsc=""><a title="https&#58;//url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/6pFCCPNK5pSDlngoizBHgUxZnDJ?domain=links-1.govdelivery.com" href="https&#58;//url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/6pFCCPNK5pSDlngoizBHgUxZnDJ?domain=links-1.govdelivery.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-auth="NotApplicable" data-linkindex="25" data-ogsc="rgb(0, 0, 238)" data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Virtual Attendee Link for June 9 Commissioners' Work Session</a></strong></li>
<li><strong data-ogsc="">Call-in information&#58; 1-833-568-8864, Webinar ID&#58; 165 543 8938</strong></li>
</ul></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV ><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem19' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H3 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem19TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >10.a</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(19);" >Work Session</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H3><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><p><span>This is a public meeting where the Board of County Commissioners receives information, reviews proposals, and discusses topics in greater detail often prior to making a decision in a later public meeting. These sessions allow commissioners and staff to explore issues, ask questions, and consider options in a collaborative setting. The BOCC does not generally take formal action or vote during a work session.&#160; No public comment will be taken.</span></p></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV ><DIV class='AgendaItemContainer indent' style="width:auto" ><DIV class='AgendaItem AgendaItem36' style="width:100%" ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitleRow' ><H4 Id='AgendaItemAgendaItem36TitleHeader' style="display: inline-block;" ><DIV class='AgendaItemCounter' style="display:inline-block;" >1.</DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemNavigate indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemTitle' style="width:auto;display:inline-block;" ><a tabindex='0' href="javascript:SelectItem(36);" >Boulder County Human Services Budget Update</a></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemCategory' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none" ></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemSponsors' ><DIV style="text-decoration:none;" ></DIV></DIV></DIV></H4><DIV class='AgendaItemIcons' style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;" ><DIV style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none" ></DIV><a href="javascript:SelectItem(36, 'attachments')" tabIndex='-1' ><img Title='Attachments'  src='./_layouts/images/eScribe/attachment.svg' alt='This item has attachments.'  role='presentation' /></a>&nbsp;<SPAN style="width:8px" ></SPAN></DIV><DIV class='visible-xs visible-sm' style=" padding:1px " ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachmentsList indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemAttachment AgendaItemAttachment36' ><SPAN class='Sequence' >1.</SPAN><a class='Link' tabindex='0' href="filestream.ashx?DocumentId=43744" data-toggle='tooltip' data-html='true' data-container='body' data-original-title='BOCC Work Session 6-9-26 HS Budget.pdf' target='_blank' ><SPAN class='Link' >BOCC Work Session 6-9-26 HS Budget.pdf</SPAN></a></DIV></DIV></DIV></DIV><DIV class='AgendaItemContentRow indent' ><DIV class='AgendaItemDescription RichText' ><DIV ><DIV ><ul>
